## Recovery Procedures

### Backup Before Changes

```bash
# On HA host
ssh david@192.168.1.110
sudo cp /opt/homeassistant/config/configuration.yaml \
       /opt/homeassistant/config/configuration.yaml.backup.$(date +%Y%m%d)

# Backup entire config directory
sudo tar -czf /home/david/ha-config-backup-$(date +%Y%m%d).tar.gz \
  /opt/homeassistant/config/
```

### Full System Recovery

If HA is completely broken:

1. **Stop container**

   ```bash
   docker stop homeassistant
   ```

2. **Restore from backup**

   ```bash
   sudo tar -xzf /home/david/ha-config-backup-YYYYMMDD.tar.gz -C /
   ```

3. **Start container**

   ```bash
   docker start homeassistant
   ```

4. **Verify**
   ```bash
   docker logs -f homeassistant
   ```

### Database Recovery

If database is corrupted:

```bash
# Stop HA
docker stop homeassistant

# Backup current DB
sudo cp /opt/homeassistant/config/home-assistant_v2.db \
       /home/david/ha_v2.db.corrupted

# Remove database (will recreate on start)
sudo rm /opt/homeassistant/config/home-assistant_v2.db

# Start HA (will create new DB)
docker start homeassistant

# Note: All history will be lost
```

